{"chapter": "conventions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0004", "placeholders": {"CITE_0001": "\\cite{Kunen}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1fb7cb4fde38cf6e4aeb233aaabe7dbebc4dfdd3e39e7df8e650b0b66f2b8fd2", "source_text": "We use Zermelo-Fraenkel set theory with the axiom of choice. See <CITE_0001>. We do not use universes (different from SGA4). We do not stress set-theoretic issues, but we make sure everything is correct (of course) and so we do not ignore them either.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:657b7e34ee24776a91549049622d0d2a68cb3b0c405978b7becf2afcef540de4", "unit_id": "tag:0004:p001"}
